# Gallant Pie-Wielder ({2}{W}, 2/3 first strike): "Celebration — This creature has double strike as long as two or more nonland
# permanents entered the battlefield under your control this turn" (CR 207.2c, 611.3a). On turn three Bot1 plays a Plains and
# casts the Pie-Wielder: one nonland permanent, first strike alone. A Memnite entering after it is the second, so it has double
# strike as well. The Mox Pearl of turn one doesn't count on turn three: at the start of turn five (Plains and Memnite make only one
# nonland permanent) it has first strike alone again, and an Ornithopter is the second.

